WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:03.133
-You look great, buddy. Thanks so much for being here.

00:00:03.133 --> 00:00:04.334
How does -- It's good to see your face.

00:00:04.334 --> 00:00:06.367
-I know, actually not on a computer screen.

00:00:06.367 --> 00:00:09.033
-In person. -Actually to feel you guys here.

00:00:09.033 --> 00:00:11.200
To walk on with that music! [ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:12.367
-You feel the energy, right?

00:00:12.367 --> 00:00:13.901
-Yeah, you can't do an interview on your show

00:00:13.901 --> 00:00:15.834
without the Roots backing you up as you walk on.

00:00:15.834 --> 00:00:17.400
It gives you confidence when you come out here.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.100
-Yes. Exactly right. -You feel like you're somebody.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:21.767
-Yeah, Zoom, go on, git! You know? Yeah.

00:00:21.767 --> 00:00:23.334
-[ Laughter ] -How's the fam, by the way?

00:00:23.334 --> 00:00:24.901
How's everybody doing? -Everybody's good.

00:00:24.901 --> 00:00:28.534
-Yeah, I saw Maya is doing fantastic.

00:00:28.534 --> 00:00:30.167
She's on "Stranger Things." -Yeah.

00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:31.501
-Maya Hawke.

00:00:31.501 --> 00:00:34.000
Did you always know she was going to be an actor?

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.267
-I knew from the time that she was about 4

00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:40.367
that she was definitely going to be an artist.

00:00:40.367 --> 00:00:42.767
Well, first of all, I don't want to hurt her feelings,

00:00:42.767 --> 00:00:44.934
but she's not good at anything else, you know?

00:00:44.934 --> 00:00:47.601
No, that's the joke in the family.

00:00:47.601 --> 00:00:51.033
But you get this young person around photography, poetry,

00:00:51.033 --> 00:00:54.267
music, acting, singing, painting, anything,

00:00:54.267 --> 00:00:57.300
she excels and she loves it and she can --

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.501
She is destined for great things, for sure.

00:00:59.501 --> 00:01:00.801
-Yeah, she can sing, too.

00:01:00.801 --> 00:01:02.667
-Oh, she's got an album coming out.

00:01:02.667 --> 00:01:04.634
Her music is phenomenal.

00:01:04.634 --> 00:01:06.100
New season of "Stranger Things" is coming out.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:07.434
So I'm not worried about her.

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:09.234
-No, no. Good, good. Good for you. Good.

00:01:09.234 --> 00:01:12.267
You told me backstage how awesome it was --

00:01:12.267 --> 00:01:14.334
You got a cool experience recently.

00:01:14.334 --> 00:01:16.901
-I had the best experience

00:01:16.901 --> 00:01:19.167
I've had on this planet breathing.

00:01:19.167 --> 00:01:20.367
-Yeah. -Yeah.

00:01:20.367 --> 00:01:22.667
I had some great times not breathing, but...

00:01:22.667 --> 00:01:24.367
-That's a different story. We'll get into that next time.

00:01:24.367 --> 00:01:25.801
-It took me by complete surprise.

00:01:25.801 --> 00:01:27.567
My son is going to college, and he said,

00:01:27.567 --> 00:01:28.767
"You know, I'm playing a gig this weekend."

00:01:28.767 --> 00:01:30.334
"You're playing a gig?"

00:01:30.334 --> 00:01:32.167
He's like, "Yeah, somebody's -- We're throwing together a band.

00:01:32.167 --> 00:01:33.400
We're going to play a show at this bar."

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:35.501
And I was like, "Can I come?"

00:01:35.501 --> 00:01:37.601
He's like, "Yeah, all right.

00:01:37.601 --> 00:01:39.667
Just stand in the back. Don't be weird."

00:01:39.667 --> 00:01:41.300
So it's like, "All right, cool, cool."

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:45.133
So I came, and not only did he blow the room away,

00:01:45.133 --> 00:01:49.133
but his sister was there backing him up singing harmony.

00:01:49.133 --> 00:01:51.701
Just -- You know, I mean, she's like a genuine rock god herself,

00:01:51.701 --> 00:01:53.334
and she's there backing him up.

00:01:53.334 --> 00:01:54.601
He's singing his own songs.

00:01:54.601 --> 00:01:55.934
He's singing other people's songs.

00:01:55.934 --> 00:01:57.367
He's rocking out.

00:01:57.367 --> 00:02:01.033
And I stood in the back, and it was like reasons to live.

00:02:01.033 --> 00:02:02.934
It's like reasons to go through a pandemic,

00:02:02.934 --> 00:02:05.167
reasons to be a human being.

00:02:05.167 --> 00:02:06.667
It doesn't get better than that.

00:02:06.667 --> 00:02:08.767
-I'm so happy, buddy. I'm so happy for you.

00:02:08.767 --> 00:02:10.334
[ Cheers and applause ] I can't wait.

00:02:10.334 --> 00:02:13.200
-It's just true. It's just true. -You were telling me that.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:16.534
I want to talk about "Moon Knight" on Disney Plus,

00:02:16.534 --> 00:02:17.901
but I also want to talk about --

00:02:17.901 --> 00:02:19.534
You were just at South by Southwest.

00:02:19.534 --> 00:02:20.667
-Yeah.

00:02:20.667 --> 00:02:22.100
-With a really, really cool project.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:24.267
-Yeah, I've got --

00:02:24.267 --> 00:02:26.467
I've taken after Questlove and I made a documentary.

00:02:26.467 --> 00:02:27.701
-That's right.

00:02:27.701 --> 00:02:30.234
-Yeah, I'm following the best documentary

00:02:30.234 --> 00:02:32.934
that has been made of all time, "Summer of Soul."

00:02:32.934 --> 00:02:34.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:34.968 --> 00:02:38.868
But, no, my pandemic project -- I've been making a documentary

00:02:38.868 --> 00:02:40.501
about Paul Newman and Joanne Woodward.

00:02:40.501 --> 00:02:42.000
-Wow. -And they --

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:45.300
For people that don't know, they have two 50-year careers,

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:46.901
you know, won every acting award.

00:02:46.901 --> 00:02:48.868
They made meaningful, substantive art.

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:52.133
They gave away over half a billion dollars.

00:02:52.133 --> 00:02:53.534
They raised a family.

00:02:53.534 --> 00:02:56.167
They are two white people who were born with a lot

00:02:56.167 --> 00:02:57.701
who did a lot with it.

00:02:57.701 --> 00:02:59.601
You can be part of the solution.

00:02:59.601 --> 00:03:01.501
And they were people that I think function

00:03:01.501 --> 00:03:02.868
as kind of a north star

00:03:02.868 --> 00:03:05.501
about what a meaningful life in the arts can look like.

00:03:05.501 --> 00:03:07.868
They're really super-inspiring people.

00:03:07.868 --> 00:03:09.534
-Legends. -Yeah, and so I've been working

00:03:09.534 --> 00:03:11.100
on that documentary, and we just showed

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:13.234
the first chapter at South by Southwest.

00:03:13.234 --> 00:03:15.000
-And that's going to air on CNN?

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.501
-On CNN in the summer.

00:03:16.501 --> 00:03:18.267
-Yeah. Dude, congrats on that.

00:03:18.267 --> 00:03:20.000
Paul Newman and Joanne, they are the greatest.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:22.167
They do so much. [ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:22.167 --> 00:03:25.501
I worked with them a little bit on our Ben &amp; Jerry's flavor.

00:03:25.501 --> 00:03:28.200
Our proceeds go to SeriousFun.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:31.567
-Which is what Hole in the Wall used to be.

00:03:31.567 --> 00:03:33.801
Paul started this camp for sick kids.

00:03:33.801 --> 00:03:35.467
It's a beautiful thing.

00:03:35.467 --> 00:03:37.300
A beautiful camp where they help children.

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:38.601
And now you're doing it. -Yeah.

00:03:38.601 --> 00:03:40.434
-Because you're a stud. -No, come on, no.

00:03:40.434 --> 00:03:43.567
I can't hold a candle to Paul Newman.

00:03:43.567 --> 00:03:46.501
-It's a powerful thing to give people who don't have much hope,

00:03:46.501 --> 00:03:47.934
to give them hope.

00:03:47.934 --> 00:03:49.467
-If you go to that website and go check out --

00:03:49.467 --> 00:03:51.167
google SeriousFun and what they do to --

00:03:51.167 --> 00:03:53.467
-You got to do it. These kids are miracles.

00:03:53.467 --> 00:03:55.734
-And he lets them raise hell. Unbelievable.

00:03:55.734 --> 00:03:57.434
I want to talk about "Moon Knight,"

00:03:57.434 --> 00:03:59.400
because everyone's so excited about this.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:03.133
You, Oscar Isaac, and -- You said that Oscar Isaac

00:04:03.133 --> 00:04:05.200
had a lot to do with you getting this part.

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:06.634
-Well, he did.

00:04:06.634 --> 00:04:08.033
It's kind of like how you and I met in a lot of ways.

00:04:08.033 --> 00:04:09.400
I mean -- -You remember that?

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:13.133
-Yeah, totally. But I digress. Okay.

00:04:13.133 --> 00:04:15.934
It was during the pandemic. We're all masked up.

00:04:15.934 --> 00:04:18.934
I go to get a cup of coffee. I'm actually with Maya.

00:04:18.934 --> 00:04:22.634
And this guy with his mask on starts talking to me,

00:04:22.634 --> 00:04:23.934
and I realize it's Oscar Isaac,

00:04:23.934 --> 00:04:25.834
and he starts telling me about "Moon Knight."

00:04:25.834 --> 00:04:27.300
And I'm like, "Cool. That sounds great."

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:28.667
He goes, "Would you be the bad guy?"

00:04:28.667 --> 00:04:31.200
I'm like, "Sure." You know?

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:32.667
I said, you know, "Call Kevin Feige

00:04:32.667 --> 00:04:34.067
and tell him to make me an offer."

00:04:34.067 --> 00:04:36.534
And I'm telling you, by dinner,

00:04:36.534 --> 00:04:37.968
I had the offer to be the bad guy.

00:04:37.968 --> 00:04:39.567
There wasn't a script yet or anything,

00:04:39.567 --> 00:04:41.367
but I just said yes because I liked Oscar.

00:04:41.367 --> 00:04:44.200
He has a fire in his eyes, this guy.

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:48.200
When you meet an actor that has a real passion for a part --

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:51.167
And I knew this was a high dive off the diving board

00:04:51.167 --> 00:04:52.501
to play a new superhero.

00:04:52.501 --> 00:04:53.734
You know, people don't know Moon Knight,

00:04:53.734 --> 00:04:56.367
and it's a really complicated character,

00:04:56.367 --> 00:04:58.300
and he was gonna go for broke, and he was telling me about it.

00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:00.234
I was like, "Mmm, I smell something great."

00:05:00.234 --> 00:05:03.033
So I did it. All that off a cup of coffee.

00:05:03.033 --> 00:05:07.968
-Yeah. With Marvel, how is that whole scene?

00:05:07.968 --> 00:05:09.801
-Well, I've spent my life making independent movies

00:05:09.801 --> 00:05:11.234
where you don't --

00:05:11.234 --> 00:05:13.267
You know, if you're supposed to have a bus,

00:05:13.267 --> 00:05:15.934
it quickly turns into, you know, "Well, we don't have a bus.

00:05:15.934 --> 00:05:17.300
We have a..." -Bicycle.

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:19.200
-Yeah, we have a bicycle or a picture of a bus

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:20.634
going by you or something.

00:05:20.634 --> 00:05:23.567
With Marvel, if you want a pyramid, you get three.

00:05:23.567 --> 00:05:25.667
If you want a crane, you get five.

00:05:25.667 --> 00:05:27.567
If you want a chopper, we got three.

00:05:27.567 --> 00:05:28.734
-Yeah.

00:05:28.734 --> 00:05:30.300
-Anything you can dream up, they make happen.

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:32.200
And so it's a little intimidating.

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:34.534
The first time I walked onto set,

00:05:34.534 --> 00:05:37.167
they were the most magnificent sets I've ever seen.

00:05:37.167 --> 00:05:39.334
You know, it was just -- and the extras

00:05:39.334 --> 00:05:41.501
and huge cameras -- -They do it right.

00:05:41.501 --> 00:05:43.000
-They do it right, man.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:44.434
So it's only you that's going to mess it up.

00:05:44.434 --> 00:05:46.734
-No, I'll never -- No, never, never, never. Yeah, exactly.

00:05:46.734 --> 00:05:48.200
Oh, I thought you meant me. Sorry.

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:50.934
No, no, me. I meant me. No, you're not going to mess it up.

00:05:50.934 --> 00:05:53.801
You're not even in the show, dude. You can relax.

00:05:53.801 --> 00:05:55.767
-They didn't let me audition. They were like,

00:05:55.767 --> 00:05:57.434
"We're good, man. We're totally fine.

00:05:57.434 --> 00:05:58.868
Yeah, we have real actors."

00:05:58.868 --> 00:06:00.567
"Sure, I can change my voice, make it deeper."

00:06:00.567 --> 00:06:02.133
They go, "No, don't do that. Don't do that."

00:06:02.133 --> 00:06:04.033
-That doesn't do it. -No, it didn't do it for me.

00:06:04.033 --> 00:06:05.667
They go, "It's more of your face, Jimmy,

00:06:05.667 --> 00:06:08.167
that we don't like."

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:10.801
Already -- The show's not even out yet,

00:06:10.801 --> 00:06:13.033
and there are already fan theories about your character,

00:06:13.033 --> 00:06:14.567
and I thought maybe you could either

00:06:14.567 --> 00:06:17.334
debunk them or maybe hint -- -Oh-oh. All right. Here we go.

00:06:17.334 --> 00:06:19.467
-This could actually get you in trouble.

00:06:19.467 --> 00:06:22.834
-All right. I signed an NDA, but let's go.

00:06:22.834 --> 00:06:24.167
-There's a fan theory

00:06:24.167 --> 00:06:27.200
that the Hulk will appear in "Moon Knight."

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:29.267
-That would be cool, right? That would be cool.

00:06:29.267 --> 00:06:30.434
Except I know Mark Ruffalo,

00:06:30.434 --> 00:06:32.234
and I think if we were in the same show,

00:06:32.234 --> 00:06:34.300
he would have at least texted me or something.

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:36.701
So I don't think that one's got a lot of legs.

00:06:36.701 --> 00:06:38.167
[ Audience groans ] I know, I know.

00:06:38.167 --> 00:06:40.334
Maybe in another one! -We didn't buy that.

00:06:40.334 --> 00:06:42.868
-Oh. They think I'm being secretive.

00:06:42.868 --> 00:06:44.367
...that whole Spider-Man stuff.

00:06:44.367 --> 00:06:45.667
-That's right. Exactly. Yeah.

00:06:45.667 --> 00:06:47.300
All right, there's a fan theory

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:49.667
that Blade will appear in "Moon Knight."

00:06:49.667 --> 00:06:51.801
[ Audience oohs ]

00:06:51.801 --> 00:06:54.901
Oh, stop. Now you're playing --

00:06:54.901 --> 00:06:57.467
Now you're just playing with me.

00:06:57.467 --> 00:06:59.667
Would you have got a text from Blade?

00:06:59.667 --> 00:07:01.634
-Yeah, I don't know. I don't know.

00:07:01.634 --> 00:07:03.734
I wish Blade was there. That would have been cool.

00:07:03.734 --> 00:07:05.000
-Okay.

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:07.601
[ Laughter ]

00:07:07.601 --> 00:07:10.734
You're good. The third one is the last one.

00:07:10.734 --> 00:07:12.567
This is my favorite fan theory.

00:07:12.567 --> 00:07:15.133
This one says, since not a lot is known about your character,

00:07:15.133 --> 00:07:17.501
Arthur Harrow, some fans speculate

00:07:17.501 --> 00:07:20.300
that Arthur Harrow is a decoy name

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:22.767
and you're actually playing the villain Dracula.

00:07:22.767 --> 00:07:25.634
[ Audience ohhs ] -That is awesome!

00:07:25.634 --> 00:07:28.667
[ Laughter ] I so want that to be true.

00:07:28.667 --> 00:07:32.067
I mean, I -- Your expectation is so intense,

00:07:32.067 --> 00:07:34.300
I want to say yes so bad.

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:35.667
I am Dracula.

00:07:35.667 --> 00:07:38.033
-Oh, wow! This is unbelievable! -You heard it here first.

00:07:38.033 --> 00:07:41.734
To hell with the lawyers! Dracula it is!

00:07:41.734 --> 00:07:44.467
-All right. So, that -- Yeah.

00:07:44.467 --> 00:07:47.033
-I want to be Dracula so bad. -Okay.

00:07:47.033 --> 00:07:48.934
Marvel watches.

00:07:48.934 --> 00:07:50.734
Yeah. So Dracula -- we can make this happen.

00:07:50.734 --> 00:07:52.334
-Write in. Write in. -Write in, everybody.

00:07:52.334 --> 00:07:54.000
We can make this work. [ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:56.234
I want to show everyone a clip. Thank you for doing that.

00:07:56.234 --> 00:07:58.767
Here's Ethan Hawke and Oscar Isaac in "Moon Knight."

00:07:58.767 --> 00:08:00.300
Take a look.

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:04.634
-We are here to make the Earth as much like heaven as possible.

00:08:04.634 --> 00:08:06.434
Who'd like to go first?

00:08:06.434 --> 00:08:09.868
♪♪

00:08:09.868 --> 00:08:13.567
You're a brave man, offering your soul for judgment,

00:08:13.567 --> 00:08:17.467
wanting to serve our goddess even before she awakes.

00:08:17.467 --> 00:08:23.501
♪♪

00:08:23.501 --> 00:08:26.667
I judge you in Ammit's name

00:08:26.667 --> 00:08:29.300
with but a fraction of her power.

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:36.868
♪♪

00:08:36.868 --> 00:08:40.901
This is the face of a good man!

00:08:40.901 --> 00:08:43.167
-Yeah! Come on!

00:08:43.167 --> 00:08:45.834
-I must warn you -- -Yes.

00:08:45.834 --> 00:08:48.968
-Not all human beings are as lucky as that dude was.

00:08:48.968 --> 00:08:50.367
There's a lot of people

00:08:50.367 --> 00:08:52.167
that don't have the face of a good man.

00:08:52.167 --> 00:08:53.334
-Yeah, exactly right.

00:08:53.334 --> 00:08:54.634
-And those sinners meet their fate.

00:08:54.634 --> 00:08:56.200
-They meet their fate. Ethan Hawke, everybody.

00:08:56.200 --> 00:09:00.367
"Moon Knight" premieres March 30th on Disney Plus.

00:09:00.367 --> 00:09:02.234
You want to conga?

00:09:02.234 --> 00:09:03.868
You feel like conga'ing out of here?

00:09:03.868 --> 00:09:05.734
Ethan, here.

00:09:05.734 --> 00:09:09.334
♪♪

00:09:09.334 --> 00:09:11.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:11.501 --> 00:09:17.200
♪♪

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:22.901
♪♪

00:09:22.901 --> 00:09:28.601
♪♪

00:09:28.601 --> 00:09:34.300
♪♪

